1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,688
We frequently misunderstand what true power is.

2
00:00:03,112 --> 00:00:04,425
We imagine tyrants,

3
00:00:04,612 --> 00:00:07,750
presidents, or billionaires with unlimited control.

4
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:08,638
However,

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,262
the most absolute foundation of power is actually

6
00:00:12,338 --> 00:00:13,500
an internal emotion—

7
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,362
the feeling of control over yourself and the

8
00:00:16,375 --> 00:00:17,500
direction of your life.

9
00:00:17,912 --> 00:00:20,450
Total powerlessness— the feeling that you have no

10
00:00:20,462 --> 00:00:22,713
voice, cannot influence your boss,

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,088
and are always a victim of circumstance—

12
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,650
is far more corrupting to the human soul

13
00:00:27,662 --> 00:00:28,675
than power itself.

14
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:31,713
Powerlessness turns people passive-aggressive,

15
00:00:31,988 --> 00:00:35,287
bitter, and fuels highly toxic psychological games.

16
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,975
To attain true power,

17
00:00:37,438 --> 00:00:39,475
you must start by taking an honest look

18
00:00:39,488 --> 00:00:40,075
in the mirror.

19
00:00:40,488 --> 00:00:43,312
Reflexively, when we hear the word narcissist,

20
00:00:43,588 --> 00:00:44,675
we point at others.

21
00:00:45,088 --> 00:00:45,525
We say,

22
00:00:45,975 --> 00:00:47,650
Oh, my boss is a narcissist,

23
00:00:47,725 --> 00:00:49,075
my ex is a narcissist,

24
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:49,900
but not me.

25
00:00:50,325 --> 00:00:50,775
Dead wrong.

26
00:00:51,188 --> 00:00:52,250
Every human being,

27
00:00:52,512 --> 00:00:55,025
by biological design and childhood trauma,

28
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:56,125
is self-centered.

29
00:00:56,538 --> 00:00:58,537
We all instinctively think of our own needs

30
00:00:58,550 --> 00:00:59,075
first.

31
00:00:59,488 --> 00:01:01,600
If you walk through life with a delusion

32
00:01:01,612 --> 00:01:03,125
of moral superiority,

33
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:06,112
feeling exempt from these primal primate traits,

34
00:01:06,412 --> 00:01:08,962
you will never possess the self-awareness to truly

35
00:01:08,975 --> 00:01:10,300
control your emotions.

36
00:01:10,712 --> 00:01:13,312
This dark side isn't something to be repressed;

37
00:01:13,638 --> 00:01:15,450
it is a wild energy that must be

38
00:01:15,462 --> 00:01:16,675
strategically channeled.

39
00:01:17,088 --> 00:01:18,962
Look at the figures we consider saints in

40
00:01:18,975 --> 00:01:19,488
history,

41
00:01:19,862 --> 00:01:22,538
like Mahatma Gandhi or Martin Luther King Jr.

42
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:25,175
Were they naive men armed only with good

43
00:01:25,188 --> 00:01:25,912
intentions?

44
00:01:26,325 --> 00:01:27,137
Absolutely not.

45
00:01:27,562 --> 00:01:29,925
They were military strategists in a different form.

46
00:01:30,338 --> 00:01:34,275
Martin Luther King consciously planned protests involving schoolchildren,

47
00:01:34,662 --> 00:01:37,288
knowing full well that brutal images of children

48
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:40,050
being attacked by police dogs would be broadcast

49
00:01:40,062 --> 00:01:41,675
across American televisions.

50
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:43,688
He knew it would break the public's heart

51
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:45,238
and force policy change.

52
00:01:45,662 --> 00:01:46,462
That was cold,

53
00:01:46,688 --> 00:01:49,312
calculated, tactical media manipulation,

54
00:01:49,688 --> 00:01:51,913
utilized for an incredibly noble cause.

55
00:01:52,325 --> 00:01:54,637
If our greatest heroes had to play strategy

56
00:01:54,762 --> 00:01:57,012
and wear masks as actors in the public

57
00:01:57,025 --> 00:01:58,438
sphere to win their battles,

58
00:01:58,725 --> 00:02:00,413
what makes you think you can succeed in

59
00:02:00,425 --> 00:02:02,638
the real world just by being yourself

60
00:02:03,188 --> 00:02:04,888
In the cutthroat professional world,

61
00:02:05,175 --> 00:02:08,275
being innocent and transparent is not a virtue;

62
00:02:08,588 --> 00:02:09,862
it is a fatal weakness.

63
00:02:10,288 --> 00:02:12,888
You must learn to separate personal emotions from

64
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,200
pragmatic execution—

65
00:02:14,612 --> 00:02:17,362
which sometimes means concealing your true intentions,

66
00:02:17,725 --> 00:02:19,650
or even hiring your old enemy for a

67
00:02:19,662 --> 00:02:21,938
better result than just working with a close

68
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:22,350
friend.
